## Why This Is Asked

This problem introduces string keys and dynamic multiset with prefix queries, common in autocomplete and search suggestions; tests correctness of trie augmentation, memory trimming, and edge cases with duplicates.

## Key Concepts

- Trie augmentation with pass and end counts
- Duplicate handling via counts
- Time/space trade-offs

## Code Example

```javascript
class TrieNode { constructor() { this.next = new Map(); this.pass = 0; this.end = 0; } }
class DynamicDictionary {
  constructor() { this.root = new TrieNode(); }
  insert(word) { let node = this.root; node.pass++; for (let ch of word) { if (!node.next.has(ch)) node.next.set(ch, new TrieNode()); node = node.next.get(ch); node.pass++; } node.end++; }
  erase(word) { let node = this.root; node.pass--; for (let ch of word) { let next = node.next.get(ch); if (!next) return; next.pass--; if (next.pass===0) node.next.delete(ch); node = next; } if (node.end>0) node.end--; }
  prefixCount(prefix) { let node = this.root; for (let ch of prefix) { if (!node.next.has(ch)) return 0; node = node.next.get(ch); } return node.pass; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle memory pressure for very large alphabets?
- How to adapt for deletion in bulk and merging branches?
